<author id="708738">LanX</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;I&gt;&amp;gt; Right, which is why &lt;C&gt;abs_path((caller)[1])&lt;/C&gt; should work in a lot of cases,&lt;/I&gt;&lt;P&gt;

Please correct me, but how is this better than &lt;C&gt;abs_path($0)&lt;/C&gt; ?&lt;P&gt;

AFAIK is &lt;C&gt;abs_path&lt;/C&gt; the problematic part, because the &lt;C&gt;CWD&lt;/C&gt; might have changed after a &lt;C&gt;chdir&lt;/C&gt; &lt;P&gt;


I suppose that $0 is even better, since [DOC://caller|&lt;tt&gt;caller&lt;/tt&gt;] might only show an intermediate module instead of the root script (untested)  &lt;P&gt;


